# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# Your Apple Developer Team ID — the ten characters in brackets in:
#   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
#
# Signing with a different team changes the app's designated requirement,
# which silently invalidates its Accessibility and Screen Recording grants:
# they keep showing as enabled in System Settings and stop working. So the
# build refuses to guess, and this has to be set once per checkout.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=

# Optional. Pick an exact certificate instead of letting the team id find it.
#ALLOWLY_SIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"

# Optional. The contact address in the VAPID token every push is signed
# with. Apple refuses a token whose subject is not a real address, so the
# default is a placeholder; set a real one if you would rather a push
# service could reach you. Can also live at
# ~/Library/Application Support/allowly/vapid-subject
#ALLOWLY_VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@your-domain.com
